<title>BELGIUM: MICHAEL ST.CLAIR-GEORGE TO BE NEW SIPEF CEO.</title>
<headline>MICHAEL ST.CLAIR-GEORGE TO BE NEW SIPEF CEO.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-08-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Michael St.Clair-George, a British national, will replace Bernard de Gerlache de Gomery as chief executive officer of Belgian plantation holding company Sipef before the end of this year, Sipef said in a statement on Tuesday.</p>
<p>De Gerlache had been Sipef CEO for seven years.</p>
<p>St. Clair-George, born in 1942, was trained as a chartered accountant. After a career in finance in Malaysia, he joined Sipef in 1991 to run its Indonesian units.</p>
